r is the change in seasons. Winter predictably follows summer, being some fifteen degrees colder in the Northern Hemisphere and five degrees colder than summer in the Southern Hemisphere. The reason the Southern Hemisphere has a smaller seasonal cycle is because it has much more ocean than land,[…]", "reference": "2003, Richard N. Cooper, Richard Layard, What the Future Holds: Insights from Social Science, MIT Press, →ISBN, page 129:"}, {"text": "the local police, who, with the investigator, reportedly placed a compass near the two signs that had rattled and found a deviation of some fifteen degrees. Placed next to the Renault in which they had come, the compass showed a deviation of only four degrees, but there was no deviation at all near the sign that had not rattled.", "reference": "2023, J. Allen Hynek, The UFO Experience: Evidence Behind Close Encounters, Project Blue Book, and the Search for Answers, Red Wheel/Weiser, →ISBN, page 142:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "около"}, {"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "приблизително"}, {"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "има-няма"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(stressed form) Emphasizing a number.", "tags": [], "examples": ["She has worked at the company for some five years now! How remarkable!"], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "цял"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(informal, stressed form) A remarkable.", "tags": ["informal"], "examples": ["He is some acrobat!", "That was some speech you gave!"], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": ["many", "much", "no"]}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "adverb", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/sʌm/", "tags": ["Received Pronunciation"]}, {